{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Units","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.lepton_continuant_recurrence"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.three_generation_windings_are_the_nonharmonic_ones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.three_generation_windings_are_the_nonharmonic_ones","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L158-L170","doc":"**Generation-exclusion summary.**  Among the four genus-admissible odd\nwindings `{3, 5, 7, 9}`, winding 9 is the unique one whose continuant\ncoefficient factors through a smaller winding's (`b₃ ∣ b₉`), while the\nprime windings `3, 5, 7` are mutually non-divisible.  This is the\nderived content of the dictionary's asserted \"(odd primes)\": the\ngenerations are the odd windings whose normal-form coefficient does not\nfactor through a smaller one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.not_b3_dvd_b7","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.not_b3_dvd_b7","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L143-L156","doc":"**Winding 7 is not a harmonic of generation 1.**  `b₇ = b₃·(X⁴+4X²+2) − 1`,\nthe same unit-remainder argument as `not_b3_dvd_b5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.not_b3_dvd_b5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.not_b3_dvd_b5","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L127-L141","doc":"**Winding 5 is not a harmonic of generation 1.**  `b₅` leaves the\nunit remainder `−1` modulo `b₃` (`b₅ = b₃·(X²+2) − 1`), so a common\ndivisor would divide `1`; but `b₃` is not a unit.  Hence `¬ (b₃ ∣ b₅)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.b3_dvd_b9","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.b3_dvd_b9","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L110-L113","doc":"`b₃ ∣ b₉` (the divisibility form of `t29_harmonic_of_first_generation`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t29_harmonic_of_first_generation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t29_harmonic_of_first_generation","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**Winding 9 is a harmonic of generation 1.**  The normal-form\n`σ`-coefficient of `T(2,9)` is the product of `T(2,3)`'s coefficient\nand the explicit cofactor `X⁶ + 6X⁴ + 9X² + 1`, so `b₃ ∣ b₉`.  This\nis the precise form of `σ⁹ = (σ³)³ factors through generation 1` on\nthe Gröbner–Shirshov normal-form data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_nine","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_nine","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L93-L96","doc":"`b₉ = X⁸ + 7X⁶ + 15X⁴ + 10X² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_seven","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L88-L91","doc":"`b₇ = X⁶ + 5X⁴ + 6X² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_five","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L83-L86","doc":"`b₅ = X⁴ + 3X² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.morganVoyceB_three","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/lepton_continuant_generation_exclusion.lean#L78-L81","doc":"`b₃ = X² + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}